+
+For report-only calls, the checker recognizes captured inputs beside the fit
+report. It prefers `project/Plex.qsf`; after normal local/remote project cleanup,
+it can read the exact `Plex.qsf` member of `inputs.tar` **without extracting it**,
+checking both the archive hash and QSF hash against the captured manifest.
+Unreadable, mismatched, ambiguous or malformed authority is refused, not
+replaced with a working-tree default. An explicitly requested QSF never falls
+back to another file/archive. Legacy report-only callers with no captured-input
+context retain baseline behavior, labeled `legacy-default`; they cannot publish
+a captured result receipt.
